  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Wu Shuai forces the gathered grotto-heaven immortals to accept him as alliance leader, then presses for an immediate next attack target. When they refuse Heavenly Court, Lady Cold Ash argues that striking Divine Emperor City would still draw Central Continent’s full resistance; he answers that luring them there would free a second group to hit Heavenly Court, then pivots again and settles on Eastern Sea’s Xia clan.",
      "chapters": [
        1981
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_wu_shuai",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "char_lady_cold_ash",
        "reg_central_continent",
        "reg_eastern_sea",
        "fac_xia_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Earlier, Lu Wei Yin had used Divine Emperor Palace for the same house.",
      "chapters": [
        1947
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lu_wei_yin",
        "house_divine_emperor_palace"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page is filed under gu-houses because Divine Emperor City is a named Immortal Gu House. It is a city-scale Immortal Gu House amalgamation, not a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ying Wu Xie, Fairy Zi Wei, and Old Man Zheng Yuan see a grand Immortal Gu House fill the sky with green light and human clamor as it moves. Old Man Zheng Yuan recalls that Divine Emperor City was created by combining Divine Bean Palace and Emperor City and had been treated as stationary at the largest gathering point of Central Continent’s human vein, then finds it can relocate that gathering point and gather Gu Immortals, Gu Masters, and mortals inside as one force, calling it likely the number one Immortal Gu House in the world. The house passes them and enters Earth Abyss.",
      "chapters": [
        2063
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "human-vein-relocation",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ying_wu_xie",
        "char_fairy_zi_wei",
        "char_old_man_zheng_yuan",
        "house_divine_bean_palace",
        "loc_emperor_city",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "reg_earth_earth_abyss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Under profound green light, Divine Emperor City leaves its original spot, flies toward Ancient Soul Sect, and enters Earth Abyss to fight Demon Immortal Qi Jue and Calamity Luck Altar. Qi Jue’s Great Qi Cloud Explosion only ripples the green light, and Bing Sai Chuan treats the house as Qin Ding Ling’s trump card. Behind it, Qin Ding Ling leads Heavenly Court Gu Immortals with several Immortal Gu Houses, Demon Judgment Board at the vanguard. Calamity Luck Altar is left by Giant Sun Immortal Venerable while Divine Emperor City is created by Genesis Lotus Immortal Venerable; in that clash Divine Emperor City wins by a huge margin and is named the number one large size Immortal Gu House in history. Spiraling green wind absorbs Qi Jue into the city despite his damaged Xi Land, then later absorbs Mao Li Qiu the same way while Calamity Luck Altar escapes.",
      "chapters": [
        2064
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "earth-abyss-clash",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_ancient_soul_sect",
        "char_demon_immortal_qi_jue",
        "house_calamity_luck_altar",
        "move_great_qi_cloud_explosion",
        "char_bing_sai_chuan",
        "char_qin_ding_ling",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "house_demon_judgment_board",
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable",
        "char_genesis_lotus_immortal_venerable",
        "loc_xi_land",
        "char_mao_li_qiu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan judges Divine Emperor City worthy of the number one Immortal Gu House even without a published ranking chart. He notes it was created by merging Divine Bean Palace and Emperor City, lacks a rank nine Immortal Gu and is not a rank nine Immortal Gu House, yet holds painting worlds from Genesis Lotus Immortal Venerable’s contented lifestyle, and he treats it as half a rank nine Immortal Gu House. He also places it as the largest gathering point of Central Continent’s human veins, a storage and cultivation ground for Central Continent geniuses, and a sacred land of human path.",
      "chapters": [
        2066
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "ranking-judgment",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Genesis Lotus’ will as the merger controller, and mobility after the fate war.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "merger-and-mobility",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fairy Zi Wei recalls that under Genesis Lotus’ will, Divine Bean Palace and Emperor City combined into Divine Emperor City, that the house stayed in Central Continent and did not move during the fate war, and that the later battle proved it could move.",
      "chapters": [
        2075
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "merger-and-mobility",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
